    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (1 test, 0 failures/errors).\n\n## What I did\n\nUnified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit`.\n\n**Identity computation** \u2014 replaced `AssignOwnerCustomerCode` + `AssignOwnerMembershipNumber` with a single `AssignOwnerMemberId` that builds `region + fy + hash8 + luhn(region+fy+hash8)`:\n- `REGION` from `Localities.ofPostcode(postcode)`\n- `FY` = 2-digit fiscal year of the (business-day-adjusted) registration date\n- `HASH8` = first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName` (the existing region-and-hash identity)\n- `CHK` = one Luhn digit over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`\n- Collision handling now scans existing `memberId`s and appends `-<n>` for uniqueness.\n\n**Field/schema removal**:\n- `Owner` \u2014 dropped `customerCode`/`membershipNumber`, added `memberId` (`member_id` column); updated `hsqldb` (test DB) and `h2` schemas.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 replaced the `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, and `membershipNumber` properties with a single `memberId` (regenerates `OwnerDto`).\n- `OwnerMapper` \u2014 removed the `checkDigit` mapping + Luhn method; repointed `locality`/`timezone`/`ownerSegment` at `memberId`.\n\n**Downstream references now use memberId**:\n- `Localities.regionOf`/`timezoneOf` \u2014 parse the leading letter run (region terminates at the FY digits) instead of splitting on `-`, since `memberId` is separator-less.\n- `AuditOwnerCreated` + `OwnerCreatedEvent` \u2014 the audit line and JSON event now carry `memberId`.\n- Updated the pipeline YAML (`owners.POST.yml`) and Javadoc cross-references in `FiscalYear`/`DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate`.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreReturnsUnifiedMemberId`) confirms the response exposes `memberId` starting with the region and containing the HASH8, with `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` gone \u2014 e.g. the audit log emitted `memberId=NSW2716E6609E1`.",
